question:
In the fourth question of Unit I, which two sets does the speaker ask to find the union of?
Choose from:
A. A = {a, b, c, d, e} and B = {c, d, e, f}
B. A = {a, b, c, d} and B = {c, d, e, f}
C. A = {a, b, c, d} and B = {d, e, f, g}
D. A = {a, b, c} and B = {c, d, e, f}
E. A = {b, c, d} and B = {c, d, e}

What are the elements of set A and set B in the question where the speaker asks the listener to find the set difference B - A?
Choose from:
A. A = {1, 2, 3, 4} and B = {2, 4, 6, 8}
B. A = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5} and B = {2, 4, 6, 8, 10}
C. A = {1, 3, 5} and B = {2, 4, 6}
D. A = {2, 3, 4} and B = {4, 6, 8}
E. A = {2, 4, 6} and B = {1, 2, 3, 4}

In the multiple assessment section of the audio, what are the elements of set E and set S specified in the question to determine the complement set S'?
Choose from:
A. E = {1, 3, 5, 7} and S = {1, 3, 5}
B. E = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6} and S = {2, 3, 4}
C. E = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5} and S = {3, 4, 5}
